For the sake of getting past solipsism I assume you are really a
consciousness outside my own, not just a figment of a dream of mine, and
hence I write this email instead of simply ignoring you. But this is a
working assumption, not an unbacked belief. It's not a belief because I
don't believe it; I don't believe anything without proof.

And whether you believe du'u or not has nothing to do with assumption.
There's no point in assuming something you already believe! Therefore the
only nontrivial case is the assumption of a fact that you don't believe.
You assume it for the sake of argument.

Hence, krici is trivially a proper subset of sruma, and otherwise a
complete fiction.



